      "message": "Thanks, `vma_page_size()` looks right here. Would you mind moving the choice into a helper in `include/linux/p3s/proc.h`, which `fs/proc/task_mmu.c` already includes, so that the change to `show_smap()` stays on one line? Something like:\n\n```\nstatic inline unsigned long p3s_vma_mmu_pagesize(struct vm_area_struct *vma)\n{\n\tif (vma_is_p3s_4k(vma))\n\t\treturn vma_page_size(vma);\n\treturn vma_mmu_pagesize(vma);\n}\n```\n\n```\n\tSEQ_PUT_DEC(\" kB\\nMMUPageSize:    \", p3s_vma_mmu_pagesize(vma));\n```\n\nIt wouldn\u0027t need a stub of its own, since `vma_is_p3s_4k()` has one. `is_vm_hugetlb_page()` isn\u0027t needed either: `hugetlbfs_file_mmap()` refuses 4KB processes, so a 4KB VMA is never a hugetlb one.\n\nThis also keeps upstream\u0027s `vma_mmu_pagesize()` for every other VMA. That changes nothing on arm64 or x86_64. powerpc, though, overrides it for ordinary VMAs to report 4K hash pages under a 64K kernel, which is the case `MMUPageSize` was added for in `3340289ddf29` (`\"mm: report the MMU pagesize in /proc/pid/smaps\"`).",
